function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    print("<div class=\"doc-detail-layout\"><main class=\"content doc-page doc-detail\"><div class=\"doc-title\"><h2>Request</h2></div><div class=\"doc-section signatures\"><h3>Capy</h3><pre>handler request : dval</pre></div><div class=\"doc-section content\"><p>Every Capy handler receives one parameter, <code>request</code>, of type <code>dval</code>. It is a snapshot of the request taken when the handler is entered — reading it never touches the network, and reading the same field twice always gives the same answer.</p><p>Read scalars through a converter with a fallback, so a key that is absent has a defined value rather than an error:</p><p>var name := string(request.query.name, {fallback: &quot;guest&quot;})\nvar page := s64(request.query.page, {fallback: 1})\nvar debug := bool(request.query.debug)</p><p>Test for presence with the <code>?</code> suffix, which is <code>true</code> when the key exists:</p><p>if request.query.token? { print(&quot;token suppliedn&quot;) }</p><h2>Fields</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Contains</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>method</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>GET</code>, <code>POST</code>, and so on</td></tr><tr><td><code>query</code></td><td>map</td><td>parsed query-string parameters</td></tr><tr><td><code>form</code></td><td>map</td><td>parsed form body parameters</td></tr><tr><td><code>params</code></td><td>map</td><td>merged query and form parameters. Form values win when keys match.</td></tr><tr><td><code>body</code></td><td>string</td><td>the raw request body</td></tr><tr><td><code>headers</code></td><td>map</td><td>request headers, lowercased with dashes: <code>content-type</code>, <code>x-request-id</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>cookies</code></td><td>map</td><td>request cookies by name</td></tr><tr><td><code>files</c")
    print("ode></td><td>array</td><td>uploaded files, each with <code>name</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>temporary_path</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>route</code></td><td>map</td><td><code>path</code>, <code>page</code>, <code>raw_path</code>, <code>valid</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>url</code></td><td>map</td><td><code>script</code>, <code>base</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>server</code></td><td>map</td><td>remaining server and CGI variables, original uppercase names</td></tr><tr><td><code>session</code></td><td>map</td><td>the current session snapshot</td></tr><tr><td><code>props</code></td><td>map</td><td>properties passed by a component caller</td></tr><tr><td><code>config</code></td><td>map</td><td>request-visible configuration, including <code>start_directory</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>connection</code></td><td>map</td><td>connection information</td></tr><tr><td><code>unit</code></td><td>string</td><td>the source path of the unit currently executing</td></tr><tr><td><code>websocket</code></td><td>map</td><td><code>connection_id</code>, <code>scope</code>, <code>opcode</code>, <code>binary</code>, <code>connections</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>call</code></td><td>map</td><td>dispatch information for the current call</td></tr><tr><td><code>out</code></td><td>map</td><td>mutable response state: <code>status</code>, <code>header</code>, <code>cookie</code>, and <code>buffer</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Headers and server variables</h2><p><code>headers</code> holds anything that arrived as an HTTP header, renamed for readability: the transport&#39;s <code>HTTP_X_REQUEST_ID</code> appears as <code>request.headers[&quot;x-request-id&quot;]</code>. <code>content-type</code> and <code>content-length</code> are included even though they arrive without the <code>HTTP_</c")
    print("ode> prefix. Use bracket syntax for these, since the names contain dashes.</p><p><code>request.config.start_directory</code> is the process start directory. It stays stable when a unit changes its current directory.</p><p><code>server</code> holds everything else — <code>QUERY_STRING</code>, <code>REMOTE_ADDR</code>, <code>SERVER_NAME</code> — under the original uppercase names. <code>method</code>, <code>route</code>, and <code>url</code> are lifted out of <code>server</code> into their own fields, so look for them there rather than in <code>server</code>.</p><h2>Reading and writing</h2><p>The snapshot is read-only except for <code>out</code>. Set <code>request.out.status</code>, <code>request.out.header</code>, <code>request.out.cookie</code>, or <code>request.out.buffer</code> to change the response. <code>print()</code> appends to the response body.</p><p>A component receives the caller&#39;s <code>props</code> for the duration of the call. Bearer restores the previous value after the call. When nested components write back the same field, the outer component write-back wins.</p></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">print(string(request.query.name, {fallback: &quot;guest&quot;}), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">if string(request.method) == &quot;POST&quot; {\n    print(&quot;saved &quot;, string(request.form.answer), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n} else {\n    print(&quot;&lt;form method=\\&quot;post\\&quot;&gt;&lt;input name=\\&quot;answer\\&quot;&gt;&lt;/form&gt;&quot;, &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"ex")
    print("ample-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">print(string(request.headers[&quot;user-agent&quot;], {fallback: &quot;unknown&quot;}), &quot;\\n&quot;)\nprint(string(request.cookies.session, {fallback: &quot;none&quot;}), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">for file := request.files {\n    print(string(file.name), &quot; &quot;, u64(file.size), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div></div><div class=\"doc-section example\"><h3>Example</h3><div class=\"example-language capy\"><h4>Capy</h4><pre class=\"example-source\">if request.query.page? {\n    print(&quot;page &quot;, s64(request.query.page, {fallback: 1}), &quot;\\n&quot;)\n} else {\n    print(&quot;no page requested\\n&quot;)\n}\n</pre></div></div></main><aside class=\"doc-section see-also\"><h3>See also</h3><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/how-to/read-request-context/\">read-request-context</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/redirect/\">redirect</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/handler/render/\">RENDER</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/handler/cli/\">CLI</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/handler/ws/\">WS</a><a class=\"related-link\" href=\"/doc/api/string/\">string</a></aside></div>")
}
